{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cdc5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c765-6a15-7930-81af-9d81d9b3108a"},"sequence":1341,"recorded_at":1780531400002677,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c771-2626-76d0-ac31-1c04b5659dc0"},"task_id":"01a0c771-2626-76d0-ac31-1c04b5659dc0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c771-2626-76d0-ac31-1c04b5659dc0","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-55-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cd /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2t4g7i/worktree && git diff 1ba06e99090e3b7bf1aa2f4865914f4080a644ed -- LOGBOOK.md | head -30; echo ...; git diff 1ba06e99090e3b7bf1aa2f4865914f4080a644ed -- LOGBOOK.md | grep -c \\\"^+\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Show my LOGBOOK delta\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex a68d055..17ced80 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -3,6 +3,15 @@\\n > Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n > Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n \\n+## 2026-09-22\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz — tmux lifecycle operations via structured commands (initial producer delivery)\\n+\\n+- SHIPPED the second `tmuxserver` leaf: `Execute` admits exactly the eight lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, restore) and refuses unknown ones; the exec adapter reconstructs the exact `tmux -S <socket> <subcommand>` vector per operation (forged binaries, flag injection, ambient discovery all refuse); the probed socket generation binds before execution (B18-B20); bodies are pure argv builders with the stable `ax pane SESSION_ID` entrypoint; effects run through the landed terminstance engine with strict per-operation deadlines, generation rechecks, and AX-side state memory, while attach/terminate/restore mirror the landed backend/fencing/axpane gates. Every mutating operation replays idempotently; uncertain receipts reconcile through status before resuming.\\n+- Battery: 173 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED (100 new second-leaf narrowing rows with per-arm killers; first leaf's 76 rows still green, shared control). AC: 33 of 33 rows (59-91) driven through production entries by named tests. Second-leaf census: Table B 24×21 (10 measured), Table C 90×11 (all unreachable), Table D 90×21 (108 measured), every measured cell with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row; singleton arms bound by B22, engine-normalized status by B23.\\n+- Full 30-command suite green firsthand on the frozen tree (gofmt, build, vet, full suite, race gate, cover, all fuzz gates, tracecheck, cataloggen, linux/windows builds, JSON check, board validate, diff check, windows vet); OUTCOME-keyed base-vs-candidate importer comparison clean (base 82 PASS retained, zero regressions). Evidence tarball with raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- Process note: a full-suite cover gate failed while the mutant harness was still running in the same tree — the cover run compiled against a planted mutant. Re-ran clean after the harness exited 0. Never run `go test` concurrently with the harness in one worktree.\\n+\\n ## 2026-09-21\\n \\n ### TASK-260830-35urbp rev7 — Commit-side O_DIRECTORY pin, WSL2 miss member, catalog-derived decoy completeness\\n@@ -2598,3 +2607,15 @@ assertion here rather than a brittle one.\\n - COVERAGE RATIO: 19 of 21 enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named production-entry tests. The two stated bounds remain: Windows runtime DACL execution is not available on this Darwin runner, and this repository has no export/replication consumer surface for host-trust secret exclusion. No claim is made for either bound.\\n - VALIDATION: grouped full suite `go test -count=1 -v` A/B/C/D all exit 0 across all 26 packages; grouped full coverage A/B/C/D all exit 0 (`config 93.5%`, `hosttrust 77.9%`, `peeridentity 97.5%`); scoped hosttrust/config/peeridentity tests, scoped vet, native/Linux-arm64/Windows-amd64 builds, Windows test compilation, `go mod tidy -diff`, and `git diff --check` are green. Logs and package inventory are in `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/`.\\n - STATUS: ready for review; worktree remains intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot.\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rework rev2 — rev1 CHANGES REQUESTED repaired on checkpoint 1ba06e9\\n+- SCOPE: second leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i, tmux lifecycle operations. All five P1 + two P2 closed in `internal/tmuxserver`; trunk unmoved, no rebase. Only touched landed files: error-code registry (new codes), ownership seam (test hook), mutant harness (new rows).\\n+- P1-A: boundary vector is the bare blocking `wait-for <channel>` (no `-L`); proof kind carried engine→evidence with provider rows as best-effort context; quiesce barrier = `lock-session` then `detach-client -s` with AX-side input-attach refusal once quiescing; no `send-keys` from quiesce. Bound B33: wrapper `wait-for -S` signal unimplemented, waits time out fail-closed.\\n+- P1-B: `BuildCommand` emits `attach-session -r` iff `input_authorized=false`; unstated authorization refuses at the execution boundary.\\n+- P1-C: `RunResult` carries stderr; signal deaths error and prove nothing; `classifyAbsence` proves absence only from exit + stderr marker (tmux 3.6a verified), everything else unknown at all three consumers (probe/poll/terminate). Bound B35: other tmux versions fail closed.\\n...\\n22\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4635,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1159,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
