gates. Every mutating operation replays idempotently; uncertain receipts reconcile through status before resuming.\\n- Battery: 173 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED (100 new second-leaf narrowing rows with per-arm killers; first leaf's 76 rows still green, shared control). AC: 33 of 33 rows (59-91) driven through production entries by named tests. Second-leaf census: Table B 24×21 (10 measured), Table C 90×11 (all unreachable), Table D 90×21 (108 measured), every measured cell with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row; singleton arms bound by B22, engine-normalized status by B23.\\n- Full 30-command suite green firsthand on the frozen tree (gofmt, build, vet, full suite, race gate, cover, all fuzz gates, tracecheck, cataloggen, linux/windows builds, JSON check, board validate, diff check, windows vet); OUTCOME-keyed base-vs-candidate importer comparison clean (base 82 PASS retained, zero regressions). Evidence tarball with raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- Process note: a full-suite cover gate failed while the mutant harness was still running in the same tree — the cover run compiled against a planted mutant. Re-ran clean after the harness exited 0. Never run `go test` concurrently with the harness in one worktree.\\n\\n=== HEAD lines 20-28 ===\\n- TRACEABILITY: route (b) owns the losing-profile registry case at `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo.go:AppendEvent`; independent lease-aware derivation-side authority is a bound owned by `STORY-260922-cpkajd` / `TASK-260922-31qyyi`, not an independent guarantee in this leaf. The case is referenced by Section 2.4 clause 2.4#2. Candidate registry digest is re-derived after that edge as `174728a8a01e8429004e4f9c4687f8fa1f17406b641012236c3427a758baf31e`; exact-tree tracecheck prints `contracts=64 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=154 fixtures=33 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0` and `section coverage: bindings=69 full=4 partial=9 sliver=9 unevidenced=43 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=70/574`. Section 2.4 admits; section 5.3 correctly refuses assigned-scope admission at 7/8 partial coverage.\\n- P3 DISPOSITIONS: the axpane `decide.go` “lapsed grants refuse” qualifier remains untouched and is scoped to the local-owner path; `observeRemoteWinner` structural redundancy is record-only; the grant-less remote interactive-owner step-4 product question remains unresolved and undecided; unknown higher epoch and empty lease-store behavior are named bounds with owners; evidence records the final candidate TREE OID in the task matrix and keeps the exact test masks beside every row count.\\n- MUTATION: the shipped harness ran twice under `mutants-append-rev3-pass1/` and `mutants-append-rev3-pass2/`. Both true reachable narrowings are KILLED twice; comment controls SURVIVE, missing-token controls are NOT_APPLIED, syntax controls are COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE, and control-before/after suites exit 0. Raw per-plant logs and exits are retained in both directories.\\n- VALIDATION: the fresh configured run is recorded under `.temp/BUG-260917-3lddu0/validation-rev3/`; all 30 configured commands exited 0. `task-board validate` reported 179 existing `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics and exited 0; scoped tracecheck §2.4 exited 0 and §5.3 exited 1 as the expected 7/8 refusal.\\n- HANDOFF: importer outcomes and tracecheck logs are task-scoped; the candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for snapshot handoff.\\n\\n## 2026-09-21\\n\\n### BUG-260917-2fwf8e — fencing direction must beat lapsed-grant refusal\\n- COVERAGE RATIO: 19 of 21 enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named production-entry tests. The two stated bounds remain: Windows runtime DACL execution is not available on this Darwin runner, and this repository has no export/replication consumer surface for host-trust secret exclusion. No claim is made for either bound.\\n- VALIDATION: grouped full suite `go test -count=1 -v` A/B/C/D all exit 0 across all 26 packages; grouped full coverage A/B/C/D all exit 0 (`config 93.5%`, `hosttrust 77.9%`, `peeridentity 97.5%`); scoped hosttrust/config/peeridentity tests, scoped vet, native/Linux-arm64/Windows-amd64 builds, Windows test compilation, `go mod tidy -diff`, and `git diff --check` are green. Logs and package inventory are in `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/`.\\n- STATUS: ready for review; worktree remains intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5301,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1326,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
