{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d10b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c765-6a15-7930-81af-9d81d9b3108a"},"sequence":1760,"recorded_at":1780531400003515,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c775-1e7e-7d51-bb41-d5fde9e81f76"},"task_id":"01a0c775-1e7e-7d51-bb41-d5fde9e81f76","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c775-1e7e-7d51-bb41-d5fde9e81f76","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/lifecycle.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"time\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axpane\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/termbind\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminstance\"\n14|)\n15|\n16|// Lifecycle executes the eight tmux lifecycle operations — create,\n17|// attach, status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, request-stop,\n18|// terminate-stale, restore — over the structured commands. Five\n19|// operations (create, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, request-stop,\n20|// status) delegate to the landed terminstance engine with the tmux\n21|// backend; attach, terminate-stale, and restore — which the engine\n22|// scope gate refuses — execute here over the same landed gates\n23|// (transition matrix, idempotency shapes, authorization, capability\n24|// conferral, receipt and binding stores) plus the tmux backend.\n25|//\n26|// A Lifecycle is constructed whole: every store and function value is\n27|// required (except Sleep/PollInterval, which default, and\n28|// ServerAdmission, which only attach needs). The Execute entry refuses\n29|// before any work when a dependency is missing.\n30|type Lifecycle struct {\n31|\t// RuntimeDir is the tmux runtime directory (<root>/tmux) the\n32|\t// socket derives from.\n33|\tRuntimeDir string\n34|\t// Root is the Runtime IPC root the socket custody verifies.\n35|\tRoot string\n36|\t// Platform selects the sun_path limit.\n37|\tPlatform scalar.Platform\n38|\t// Runner executes the tmux commands.\n39|\tRunner Runner\n40|\t// Receipts is the durable idempotency receipt table.\n41|\tReceipts *terminstance.ReceiptStore\n42|\t// Bindings is the durable bootstrap binding store.\n43|\tBindings *axpane.Store\n44|\t// Attach is the durable attach-client receipt store.\n45|\tAttach *termbind.AttachStore\n46|\t// States is the durable AX-side state memory.\n47|\tStates *InstanceStates\n48|\t// CurrentLease and CurrentGeneration re-read the winning lease\n49|\t// and the validated binding generation at every check point.\n50|\tCurrentLease      func() terminstance.LeaseView\n51|\tCurrentGeneration func() string\n52|\t// Now is the clock.\n53|\tNow func() time.Time\n54|\t// Sleep waits between close-confirm polls. Nil means time.Sleep.\n55|\tSleep func(time.Duration)\n56|\t// PollInterval separates close-confirm polls. Non-positive means\n57|\t// 50 milliseconds.\n58|\tPollInterval time.Duration\n59|\t// ServerAdmission reports the live server attestation the attach\n60|\t// handler binds to the request generation (the P3-A wiring: a\n61|\t// fresh decoy admission refuses here). Nil refuses attach only.\n62|\tServerAdmission func() (RealmAdmission, error)\n63|\t// LocalHostID is the AX host identity the after-restore branch\n64|\t// compares the winning lease holder against. Empty cannot prove\n65|\t// a local win, so restores report parked or a remote offer only.\n66|\tLocalHostID string\n67|\t// LeaseRefresh attempts the §4.2 mesh lease refresh (after-restore\n68|\t// step 2) under a timeout context. Nil skips the attempt and the\n69|\t// branch decides over the locally known lease. A failed attempt\n70|\t// also falls back to local knowledge: the refresh is attempted,\n71|\t// never required.\n72|\tLeaseRefresh func(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) (RefreshWinner, error)\n73|\t// MeshRefreshTimeout bounds one refresh attempt. Non-positive\n74|\t// means DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout. The bound is measured, not\n75|\t// advisory: the refresh context carries exactly this deadline.\n76|\tMeshRefreshTimeout time.Duration\n77|\t// Materialization reports whether the required materialization\n78|\t// for a restore checkpoint is valid (after-restore step 3). Nil\n79|\t// reports invalid: local resume requires positive proof.\n80|\tMaterialization func(sessionID, checkpointID string) (bool, error)\n81|\t// Hooks observes receipts and effects. Nil disables observation.\n82|\tHooks *terminstance.EngineHooks\n83|}\n84|\n85|// DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout bounds the after-restore mesh lease\n86|// refresh when the Lifecycle leaves it unset: five seconds, after\n87|// which the branch proceeds on local knowledge instead of blocking\n88|// forever.\n89|const DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout = 5 * time.Second\n90|\n91|// RefreshWinner is one mesh lease-refresh answer: the winning lease\n92|// tuple and its holder host.\n93|type RefreshWinner struct {\n94|\tLeaseID      string\n95|\tEpoch        uint64\n96|\tHolderHostID string\n97|}\n98|\n99|// After-restore branch actions: the §4.2 steps 3-5 outcome the\n100|// restore entry reports alongside the parked wire result.\n101|const (\n102|\t// AfterRestoreResumed reports a local resume: the local host\n103|\t// holds the winning lease and the materialization is valid.\n104|\tAfterRestoreResumed = \"resumed_locally\"\n105|\t// AfterRestoreRemoteOffer reports a remote offer: another host\n106|\t// owns the session and the restore runs in an interactive\n107|\t// terminal.\n108|\tAfterRestoreRemoteOffer = \"remote_offered\"\n109|\t// AfterRestoreParked reports parked: every other case, with no\n110|\t// provider launched.\n111|\tAfterRestoreParked = \"parked\"\n112|)\n113|\n114|// AfterRestoreOutcome is the restore entry's §4.2 branch report: the\n115|// winning lease the branch decided over, whether the mesh refresh\n116|// was attempted, the measured refresh bound in milliseconds, and the\n117|// action. The backend never launches a provider on any branch — the\n118|// wrapper owns launch gating through its own decision — so this\n119|// report steers the caller, never a local provider.\n120|type AfterRestoreOutcome struct {\n121|\tAction           string\n122|\tWinnerLeaseID    string\n123|\tWinnerHostID     string\n124|\tRefreshAttempted bool\n125|\tRefreshBoundMs   uint64\n126|}\n127|\n128|// OpRequest is one lifecycle operation request: the operation name,\n129|// its closed body, the presented source state, the admitted\n130|// capabilities, the fencing material (for terminate-stale only), and\n131|// the interactive flag (for restore only: whether the restore runs in\n132|// an interactive terminal, which selects the remote-offer branch).\n133|type OpRequest struct {\n134|\tOperation            string\n135|\tBody                 []byte\n136|\tSource               string\n137|\tAdmitted             terminalbackend.Admitted\n138|\tPresented            fencing.PresentedToken\n139|\tWinner               sessrepo.LeaseSummary\n140|\tHasWinner            bool\n141|\tForceRecovery        bool\n142|\tDiagnosticsPreserved bool\n143|\tInteractive          bool\n144|}\n145|\n146|// AttachOutcome is the attach success payload: the client mirror, the\n147|// host-local descriptor, the authorized input boolean, and the\n148|// evidence. The result input boolean always equals the request and the\n149|// authorization; the landed CheckAttachResult proves it on every call.\n150|type AttachOutcome struct {\n151|\tClientMirrorID  string\n152|\tDescriptor      string\n153|\tInputAuthorized bool\n154|\tEvidenceIDs     []string\n155|}\n156|\n157|// OpOutcome is one executed operation: exactly one of Mutation,\n158|// Status, or Attach is set, plus the per-operation success members.\n159|// Mutation is set on every executed mutating path — success and\n160|// coded failure alike, mirroring the engine — and nil only when the\n161|// request was malformed before any result existed.\n162|type OpOutcome struct {\n163|\tOperation              terminalbackend.Operation\n164|\tMutation               *terminstance.Result\n165|\tStatus                 *terminstance.StatusReport\n166|\tAttach                 *AttachOutcome\n167|\tArgv                   []string\n168|\tBinding                *termbind.Binding\n169|\tDescriptor             *string\n170|\tPriorBindingID         string\n171|\tRestoredParked         bool\n172|\tAfterRestore           *AfterRestoreOutcome\n173|\tTargetClosed           bool\n174|\tProcessClosed          bool\n175|\tStoreClosed            bool\n176|\tQuiescenceGeneration   string\n177|\tInputClosedAt          string\n178|\tSafeBoundaryEvidenceID string\n179|\tBoundaryObservedAt     string\n180|}\n181|\n182|// Execute runs one lifecycle operation to its outcome. Refusals\n183|// precede side effects: malformed operations, unknown backends, and\n184|// unsafe sockets refuse before any store or tmux interaction. The\n185|// socket custody (before-connect rejection) and length refusal run on\n186|// every operation, because every operation connects.\n187|func (lc *Lifecycle) Execute(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest) (OpOutcome, error) {\n188|\tempty := OpOutcome{}\n189|\tif lc == nil || lc.Runner == nil || lc.Receipts == nil || lc.Bindings == nil ||\n190|\t\tlc.Attach == nil || lc.States == nil ||\n191|\t\tlc.CurrentLease == nil || lc.CurrentGeneration == nil || lc.Now == nil {\n192|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle dependencies\"}\n193|\t}\n194|\toperation, err := terminalbackend.ParseOperation(req.Operation)\n195|\tif err != nil {\n196|\t\treturn empty, err\n197|\t}\n198|\tif _, err := DirectivesFor(operation); err != nil {\n199|\t\treturn empty, err\n200|\t}\n201|\tsocket := SocketPath(lc.RuntimeDir)\n202|\tif err := CheckSocketLength(socket, lc.Platform); err != nil {\n203|\t\treturn empty, err\n204|\t}\n205|\tif err := CheckSocketCustody(socket, lc.Root, lc.Platform); err != nil {\n206|\t\treturn empty, err\n207|\t}\n208|\tswitch operation {\n209|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationCreate:\n210|\t\treturn lc.executeCreate(ctx, req, socket)\n211|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationAttach:\n212|\t\treturn lc.executeAttach(ctx, req, socket)\n213|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationStatus:\n214|\t\treturn lc.executeStatus(ctx, req, socket)\n215|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput:\n216|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n217|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\n218|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n219|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n220|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n221|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationTerminateStale:\n222|\t\treturn lc.executeTerminate(ctx, req, socket)\n223|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRestore:\n224|\t\treturn lc.executeRestore(ctx, req, socket)\n225|\tdefault:\n226|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle operation\"}\n227|\t}\n228|}\n229|\n230|// engineFor builds the per-call landed engine over a request-scoped\n231|// tmux backend. The engine is a plain struct: constructing one per\n232|// call keeps request identity out of shared state.\n233|func (lc *Lifecycle) engineFor(reqBackend *backend) *terminstance.Engine {\n234|\treturn &terminstance.Engine{\n235|\t\tStore:             lc.Receipts,\n236|\t\tBackend:           reqBackend,\n237|\t\tCurrentLease:      lc.CurrentLease,\n238|\t\tCurrentGeneration: lc.CurrentGeneration,\n239|\t\tNow:               lc.Now,\n240|\t\tHooks:             lc.Hooks,\n241|\t}\n242|}\n243|\n244|// requestBackend builds the request-scoped tmux backend over the\n245|// lifecycle stores and the admitted set.\n246|func (lc *Lifecycle) requestBackend(req OpRequest, socket, session, instance string) *backend {\n247|\tsleep := lc.Sleep\n248|\tif sleep == nil {\n249|\t\tsleep = time.Sleep\n250|\t}\n251|\tpoll := lc.PollInterval\n252|\tif poll <= 0 {\n253|\t\tpoll = 50 * time.Millisecond\n254|\t}\n255|\treturn &backend{\n256|\t\trunner:     lc.Runner,\n257|\t\truntimeDir: lc.RuntimeDir,\n258|\t\tsocket:     socket,\n259|\t\tsessionID:  session,\n260|\t\tinstanceID: instance,\n261|\t\tnow:        lc.Now,\n262|\t\tsleep:      sleep,\n263|\t\tpoll:       poll,\n264|\t\tadmitted:   req.Admitted,\n265|\t\tbindings:   lc.Bindings,\n266|\t\tattach:     lc.Attach,\n267|\t\tstates:     lc.States,\n268|\t\tkillExit:   -1,\n269|\t}\n270|}\n271|\n272|// recordAfter records the adopted after-state in the AX-side memory on\n273|// every executed path. The memory is advisory: the idempotency receipt\n274|// is the commit, and a failed Record leaves later status reads to\n275|// reconcile from live presence — so a Record failure never fails the\n276|// operation it follows, and a hook-staged failure test pins exactly\n277|// that specified behavior.\n278|func (lc *Lifecycle) recordAfter(instance string, after terminalbackend.InstanceState) {\n279|\tif lc.States == nil {\n280|\t\treturn\n281|\t}\n282|\t_ = lc.States.Record(instance, after)\n283|}\n284|\n285|// mutationResult assembles a lifecycle result with the engine's\n286|// buildResult contract: repeated request identities, before/after\n287|// states, bytewise-sorted effects and evidence, and one disposition.\n288|func mutationResult(mctx terminstance.MutationContext, before, after terminalbackend.InstanceState, effects []terminalbackend.SideEffect, evidence []string, disposition terminstance.RetryDisposition) terminstance.Result {\n289|\treturn terminstance.Result{\n290|\t\tOperationID:           mctx.OperationID,\n291|\t\tSessionID:             mctx.SessionID,\n292|\t\tTerminalInstanceID:    mctx.TerminalInstanceID,\n293|\t\tTerminalBackendID:     mctx.TerminalBackendID,\n294|\t\tImplementationVersion: mctx.ImplementationVersion,\n295|\t\tProtocolVersion:       mctx.ProtocolVersion,\n296|\t\tBackendGeneration:     mctx.BackendGeneration,\n297|\t\tBefore:                before,\n298|\t\tAfter:                 after,\n299|\t\tEffects:               sortedEffects(effects),\n300|\t\tEvidenceIDs:           sortedEvidence(evidence),\n301|\t\tDisposition:           disposition,\n302|\t}\n303|}\n304|\n305|// checkLifecycleBackend admits exactly the tmux backend identity: this\n306|// lifecycle executes for ax.tmux and no other backend. A request\n307|// naming any other backend refuses the failed local precondition,\n308|// never executes against the wrong backend.\n309|func checkLifecycleBackend(backendID string) error {\n310|\tif backendID != terminalbackend.BuiltinTmux {\n311|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"lifecycle backend\"}\n312|\t}\n313|\treturn nil\n314|}\n315|\n316|// checkBindingAgreement binds the create binding to its mutation\n317|// context: session, instance, backend, and generation must all agree.\n318|// Any disagreement refuses the failed local precondition: the binding\n319|// names another creation.\n320|func checkBindingAgreement(body CreateBody) error {\n321|\tif body.Binding.SessionID != body.Context.SessionID ||\n322|\t\tbody.Binding.TerminalInstanceID != body.Context.TerminalInstanceID ||\n323|\t\tbody.Binding.TerminalBackendID != body.Context.TerminalBackendID ||\n324|\t\tbody.Binding.BackendGeneration != body.Context.BackendGeneration {\n325|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"create binding agreement\"}\n326|\t}\n327|\treturn nil\n328|}\n329|\n330|// rowError normalizes a backend- or store-reported code against one\n331|// operation's allowed set: an in-row code propagates with its report,\n332|// while an outside-set code is itself refused as the protocol error —\n333|// the engine's CheckErrorAllowed arm, mirrored for the operations the\n334|// engine scope leaves out.\n335|func rowError(operation terminalbackend.Operation, err error) error {\n336|\tcode := backendErrorCode(err)\n337|\tif code == \"\" {\n338|\t\treturn err\n339|\t}\n340|\tif checkErr := terminalbackend.CheckErrorAllowed(string(operation), code); checkErr != nil {\n341|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"operation error vocabulary\"}\n342|\t}\n343|\treturn err\n344|}\n345|\n346|// formatTimestamp renders Now in the scalar timestamp grammar: UTC\n347|// RFC3339 with millisecond precision, always carrying the fractional\n348|// digits the grammar requires.\n349|func formatTimestamp(now time.Time) string {\n350|\treturn now.UTC().Format(\"2006-01-02T15:04:05.000Z07:00\")\n351|}\n352|\n353|// executeCreate runs the full create body: closed-shape admission,\n354|// backend and transport gates, binding agreement, then the landed\n355|// engine with the tmux backend. The result echoes the carried binding\n356|// and, exactly when interactive, the unbound attach descriptor.\n357|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeCreate(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n358|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationCreate}\n359|\tbody, err := parseCreateBody(req.Body)\n360|\tif err != nil {\n361|\t\treturn empty, err\n362|\t}\n363|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.Context.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n364|\t\treturn empty, err\n365|\t}\n366|\tif body.Transport == string(terminalbackend.TransportThirdPartyRelay) {\n367|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeUnauthorized, Detail: \"create relay transport\"}\n368|\t}\n369|\tif err := checkBindingAgreement(body); err != nil {\n370|\t\treturn empty, err\n371|\t}\n372|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.Context.SessionID, body.Context.TerminalInstanceID)\n373|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationCreate\n374|\treqBackend.bootstrapID = body.BootstrapOperationID\n375|\treqBackend.bindingID = body.Binding.BindingID\n376|\treqBackend.bindingDoc = append([]byte(nil), body.BindingRaw...)\n377|\tresult, err := lc.engineFor(reqBackend).ExecuteMutating(ctx, terminalbackend.OperationCreate, body.Context, terminstance.Params{\n378|\t\tBootstrapOperationID: body.BootstrapOperationID,\n379|\t\tInteractive:          body.Interactive,\n380|\t}, terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source), req.Admitted)\n381|\toutcome := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationCreate, Binding: &body.Binding}\n382|\tif result.OperationID != \"\" {\n383|\t\toutcome.Mutation = &result\n384|\t\tlc.recordAfter(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, result.After)\n385|\t}\n386|\tif err != nil {\n387|\t\treturn outcome, err\n388|\t}\n389|\tif body.Interactive {\n390|\t\tdescriptor := createDescriptor(socket, body.Context.TerminalInstanceID)\n391|\t\toutcome.Descriptor = &descriptor\n392|\t}\n393|\treturn outcome, nil\n394|}\n395|\n396|// executeStatus runs one status query through the landed engine with\n397|// the tmux backend: no receipt, no side effects, no authorization.\n398|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeStatus(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n399|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationStatus}\n400|\tbody, err := terminstance.ParseStatusBody(req.Body)\n401|\tif err != nil {\n402|\t\treturn empty, err\n403|\t}\n404|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n405|\t\treturn empty, err\n406|\t}\n407|\tinstance := body.TerminalInstanceID\n408|\tif !body.HasTerminalInstanceID {\n409|\t\tinstance = \"\"\n410|\t}\n411|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.SessionID, instance)\n412|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationStatus\n413|\treport, err := lc.engineFor(reqBackend).ExecuteStatus(ctx, body, terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source), req.Admitted)\n414|\tif err != nil {\n415|\t\treturn empty, err\n416|\t}\n417|\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationStatus, Status: &report}, nil\n418|}\n419|\n420|// executeEngineOp runs one quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, or\n421|// request-stop body through the landed engine with the tmux backend,\n422|// adding the per-operation success members the engine's receipt scope\n423|// leaves out.\n424|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeEngineOp(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string, operation terminalbackend.Operation) (OpOutcome, error) {\n425|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: operation}\n426|\tmctx, params, err := terminstance.ParseOperationBody(string(operation), req.Body)\n427|\tif err != nil {\n428|\t\treturn empty, err\n429|\t}\n430|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(mctx.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n431|\t\treturn empty, err\n432|\t}\n433|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, mctx.SessionID, mctx.TerminalInstanceID)\n434|\treqBackend.operation = operation\n435|\tswitch operation {\n436|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\n437|\t\treqBackend.quiescence = params.QuiescenceGeneration\n438|\t\treqBackend.channel = BoundaryChannelPrefix + params.QuiescenceGeneration\n439|\t\treqBackend.proofKind = params.ProviderProofKind\n440|\t\twaitCtx, cancel := lc.boundWait(ctx, mctx, params.TimeoutMs)\n441|\t\tdefer cancel()\n442|\t\treqBackend.waitCtx = waitCtx\n443|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n444|\t\treqBackend.deadline = lc.lesserDeadline(mctx, params.GracefulTimeoutMs)\n445|\t}\n446|\tresult, err := lc.engineFor(reqBackend).ExecuteMutating(ctx, operation, mctx, params, terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source), req.Admitted)\n447|\toutcome := OpOutcome{Operation: operation}\n448|\tif result.OperationID != \"\" {\n449|\t\toutcome.Mutation = &result\n450|\t\tlc.recordAfter(mctx.TerminalInstanceID, result.After)\n451|\t}\n452|\tif err != nil {\n453|\t\treturn outcome, err\n454|\t}\n455|\tswitch operation {\n456|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput:\n457|\t\toutcome.QuiescenceGeneration = params.QuiescenceGeneration\n458|\t\toutcome.InputClosedAt = lc.reportInputClosedAt(mctx.IdempotencyKey)\n459|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\n460|\t\t// The boundary transition carries exactly one effect, and the\n461|\t\t// engine evidences every committed effect exactly once, so a\n462|\t\t// successful boundary result carries exactly one evidence ID.\n463|\t\toutcome.SafeBoundaryEvidenceID = result.EvidenceIDs[0]\n464|\t\toutcome.BoundaryObservedAt = lc.reportBoundaryObservedAt(mctx.IdempotencyKey)\n465|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n466|\t\toutcome.ProcessClosed = true\n467|\t\toutcome.StoreClosed = true\n468|\t}\n469|\treturn outcome, nil\n470|}\n471|\n472|// reportInputClosedAt replays the recorded input-closed time for one\n473|// quiesce key, recording the current time on first success. The\n474|// receipt is already complete, so a record failure still reports the\n475|// computed time: the retry re-records rather than failing a\n476|// committed effect.\n477|func (lc *Lifecycle) reportInputClosedAt(key string) string {\n478|\tif stored, found, err := lc.States.LookupOutcome(key); err == nil && found {\n479|\t\treturn stored.InputClosedAt\n480|\t}\n481|\trendered := formatTimestamp(lc.Now())\n482|\t_ = lc.States.RecordOutcome(key, OperationOutcome{Operation: string(terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput), InputClosedAt: rendered})\n483|\treturn rendered\n484|}\n485|\n486|// reportBoundaryObservedAt replays the recorded boundary-observed\n487|// time for one boundary key, recording the current time on first\n488|// success, with the same commit-then-report discipline as the\n489|// quiesce report.\n490|func (lc *Lifecycle) reportBoundaryObservedAt(key string) string {\n491|\tif stored, found, err := lc.States.LookupOutcome(key); err == nil && found {\n492|\t\treturn stored.BoundaryObservedAt\n493|\t}\n494|\trendered := formatTimestamp(lc.Now())\n495|\t_ = lc.States.RecordOutcome(key, OperationOutcome{Operation: string(terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary), BoundaryObservedAt: rendered})\n496|\treturn rendered\n497|}\n498|\n499|// boundWait bounds the safe-boundary wait by the lesser of the request\n500|// deadline and the timeout: the wait context carries the minimum, and\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
