{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000debb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c765-6a15-7930-81af-9d81d9b3108a"},"sequence":3512,"recorded_at":1780531400007019,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c785-4840-7121-a1ad-068dca715c5b"},"task_id":"01a0c785-4840-7121-a1ad-068dca715c5b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c785-4840-7121-a1ad-068dca715c5b","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 63-83\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-\t// LocalHostID is the AX host identity the after-restore branch\n-\t// compares the winning lease holder against. Empty cannot prove\n-\t// a local win, so restores report parked or a remote offer only.\n-\tLocalHostID string\n-\t// LeaseRefresh attempts the §4.2 mesh lease refresh (after-restore\n-\t// step 2) under a timeout context. Nil skips the attempt and the\n-\t// branch decides over the locally known lease. A failed attempt\n-\t// also falls back to local knowledge: the refresh is attempted,\n-\t// never required.\n-\tLeaseRefresh func(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) (RefreshWinner, error)\n-\t// MeshRefreshTimeout bounds one refresh attempt. Non-positive\n-\t// means DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout. The bound is measured, not\n-\t// advisory: the refresh context carries exactly this deadline.\n-\tMeshRefreshTimeout time.Duration\n-\t// Materialization reports whether the required materialization\n-\t// for a restore checkpoint is valid (after-restore step 3). Nil\n-\t// reports invalid: local resume requires positive proof.\n-\tMaterialization func(sessionID, checkpointID string) (bool, error)\n-\t// Hooks observes receipts and effects. Nil disables observation.\n-\tHooks *terminstance.EngineHooks\n-}\n+\t// LocalHostID is the AX host identity the after-restore\n+\t// composition compares the winning lease holder against. Empty\n+\t// cannot prove a local win, so the composition parks or offers\n+\t// remote attach only, never resumes.\n+\tLocalHostID string\n+\t// LeaseRefresh attempts the §4.2 mesh lease refresh\n+\t// (after-restore step 2) under a timeout context. Nil skips the\n+\t// attempt; a failed attempt also falls back to local knowledge.\n+\t// Only a successful refresh verifies: the fallback decides\n+\t// unverified, so it parks instead of resuming.\n+\tLeaseRefresh func(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) (RefreshWinner, error)\n+\t// MeshRefreshTimeout bounds one refresh attempt. Non-positive\n+\t// means DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout. The bound is measured, not\n+\t// advisory: the refresh context carries exactly this deadline.\n+\tMeshRefreshTimeout time.Duration\n+\t// Hooks observes receipts and effects. Nil disables observation.\n+\tHooks *terminstance.EngineHooks\n+}\n","final_result":true}}}
