uses. Kill path: the timeless retry succeeds with an empty timestamp through the quiesce dispatch. [exit 1]\\nok: N-quiesce-report-record: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture quiesce key past the record-failure arm into an unrecorded time; the boundary crash twin still refuses. Kill path: the crashed first attempt reports instead of refusing through the quiesce dispatch. [exit 1]\\nok: N-boundary-report-corrupt: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture boundary key past the corrupt-read arm into a fresh time; the quiesce twin still refuses. Kill path: the corrupt retry reports a fresh observed time through the boundary dispatch. [exit 1]\\nok: N-boundary-report-empty: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture boundary key past the timeless-record arm; the quiesce twin still refuses. Kill path: the timeless retry succeeds with an empty timestamp through the boundary dispatch. [exit 1]\\nok: N-boundary-report-record: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture boundary key past the record-failure arm into an unrecorded time; the quiesce crash twin still refuses. Kill path: the crashed first attempt reports instead of refusing through the boundary dispatch. [exit 1]\\nok: N-outcome-key-forged: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the forged key past the lookup key arm (reviewer R2 shape); every other key still compares. Kill path: the forged document replays at the store entry and through the quiesce retry alike. [exit 1]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2203,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 551,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
