|\n499|| pollbound (backend.go:300) | U1 | U1 | U1 | B29 lesser-fed; boundary unmeasured | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | B29 past-deadline pinned; boundary unmeasured | U1 | U1 |\n500|\n501|Symmetry (every gate on two or more sides, with admitting-row\n502|counts per side; \"shared\" marks one row killing through several\n503|entries, attribution verified per entry from the raw logs):\n504|directive CMD 1 / PDIR 1 shared; scrub OSR 2 / UNT 2 shared; cmdident\n505|CMD 3 members; cmdvector EXC 1 / EXA 1 / EXE 1 / EXR 1 / CMD 4;\n506|directives 6 EX + DIRV shared 1; effectvocab/exitrefused/transport\n507|single-sided at PFX; reconfirm/escalation/persistmap/attachmap\n508|single-sided at PFX; boundarywait EXE 1 / PFX 1 shared; staterecord\n509|REC 2 members; statelookup LOOK 2 members; entrypoint/transportvocab\n510|single-sided at UNT; absentmemory EXS 1 / CLS 1 shared; presentmemory\n511|EXS 1 / CLS 1 / OBSP 1 shared; attachable EXS 1 / CLS 1 shared; cutrow\n512|OBSP 1 / UNT 1 shared (EXS B23); triple EXS 1 / UNT 1 shared; dialstale\n513|DIAL 2 members; probedeps PRB 2 members; sunpath LEN 1 / 6 EX 1 /\n514|PRB 1 shared; placement CUS 1 / PRB 1 shared; leafdelegate CUS 1 (B32\n515|propagation elsewhere); leafwiring CUS 2 sites; rootwrite CUS 1 / EXS\n516|1 / EXR 1; ancestorwrite CUS 1 / EXS 1 / EXR 1; ancestorkind CUS 1 /\n517|PRB 1 / SPW 1 shared; backendid 6 EX shared 1; agreement EXC 4\n518|members; enginemembers EXE 4 members; attachcap EXA 2 members;\n519|attestation EXA 1 + pinned member; authkind EXT 2 / EXR 2; generation\n520|EXT 1 / EXR 2; deadline EXA 1 / EXT 1 / EXR 2; keymaterial EXT 1 / EXR\n521|1; capdual EXT 2 members; fencingmap EXT 2 + 3 pinned; target EXT 3\n522|members; winner EXT 2 members (session arm U3: fencing+target\n523|precede); record EXT 1 / EXR 1 shared + UNT 1; replay EXT 2 + 6\n524|pinned; bindmap/bindfound single-sided at EXT; readonly EXA 1 / CMD 1\n525|shared; detachvec CMD 1; boundarykind/boundexit EXE 1 each + PFX\n526|0/1; quiescedetach EXE 1 / PFX 1 shared; nosendkeys/closeexit EXE 1\n527|each; probemarker EXS 1 / EXE 1 / EXT 1 shared; probeneg EXE 1;\n528|identity CUS 1; bindcontract/restoreagree EXR 1 each; replaytime EXE\n529|2; afterRestoreBranch holder/tuple/material/remote/offer/bound 1\n530|each (all EXR); refreshbound EXR 1; outcomekey REC 1 / LOOK 0 (B22\n531|singleton); binddocid REC 1 / LOOK 1; binddocshape REC 1; docpersist\n532|EXR 1; Table B verify 9 new-entry sides shared 1, server EXA 1 (its\n533|other sides are first-leaf symmetry).\n534|\n535|Ratio: 208 measured of 4448 (50+10+148 M across Tables A/B/D;\n536|Table C all U); 34 bound; 4206 unreachable with reasons. Every\n537|driven refusal direction is measured except the bound cells: 22\n538|driven but rowless (B22 singletons/forks, B23 normalized details,\n539|B29 poll past-deadline, B32 propagation) and 8 named undriven gaps\n540|(B24/B25/B26/B28/B31 cells, B29 dispatch side), each with its owner\n541|below.\n542|\n543|## Stated bounds\n544|\n545|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n546|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n547|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n548|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n549|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n550|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n551|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n552|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n553|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n554|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n555|  panic kill.\n556|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n557|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n558|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n559|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n560|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n561|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n562|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n563|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n564|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
