{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000fe6b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c765-6a15-7930-81af-9d81d9b3108a"},"sequence":7568,"recorded_at":1780531400015131,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481"},"call_id":"call_01a0c7b29ca37692bc86f2f5aab200e0","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(504 line(s) above)\n505|Symmetry (every gate on two or more sides, with admitting-row\n506|counts per side; \"shared\" marks one row killing through several\n507|entries, attribution verified per entry from the raw logs):\n508|directive CMD 1 / PDIR 1 shared; scrub OSR 2 / UNT 2 shared; cmdident\n509|CMD 3 members; cmdvector EXC 1 / EXA 1 / EXE 1 / EXR 1 / CMD 4;\n510|directives 6 EX + DIRV shared 1; effectvocab/exitrefused/transport\n511|single-sided at PFX; reconfirm/escalation/persistmap/attachmap\n512|single-sided at PFX; boundarywait EXE 1 / PFX 1 shared; staterecord\n513|REC 2 members; statelookup LOOK 2 members; entrypoint/transportvocab\n514|single-sided at UNT; absentmemory EXS 1 / CLS 1 shared; presentmemory\n515|EXS 1 / CLS 1 / OBSP 1 shared; attachable EXS 1 / CLS 1 shared; cutrow\n516|OBSP 1 / UNT 1 shared (EXS B23); triple EXS 1 / UNT 1 shared; dialstale\n517|DIAL 2 members; probedeps PRB 2 members; sunpath LEN 1 / 6 EX 1 /\n518|PRB 1 shared; placement CUS 1 / PRB 1 shared; leafdelegate CUS 1 (B32\n519|propagation elsewhere); leafwiring CUS 2 sites; rootwrite CUS 1 / EXS\n520|1 / EXR 1; ancestorwrite CUS 1 / EXS 1 / EXR 1; ancestorkind CUS 1 /\n521|PRB 1 / SPW 1 shared; backendid 6 EX shared 1; agreement EXC 4\n522|members; enginemembers EXE 4 members; attachcap EXA 2 members;\n523|attestation EXA 1 + pinned member; authkind EXT 2 / EXR 2; generation\n524|EXT 1 / EXR 2; deadline EXA 1 / EXT 1 / EXR 2; keymaterial EXT 1 / EXR\n525|1; capdual EXT 2 members; fencingmap EXT 2 + 3 pinned; target EXT 3\n526|members; winner EXT 2 members (session arm U3: fencing+target\n527|precede); record EXT 1 / EXR 1 shared + UNT 1; replay EXT 2 + 6\n528|pinned; bindmap/bindfound single-sided at EXT; readonly EXA 1 / CMD 1\n529|shared; detachvec CMD 1; boundarykind/boundexit EXE 1 each + PFX\n530|0/1; quiescedetach EXE 1 / PFX 1 shared; nosendkeys/closeexit EXE 1\n531|each; probemarker EXS 1 / EXE 1 / EXT 1 shared; probeneg EXE 1;\n532|identity CUS 1; bindcontract/restoreagree EXR 1 each; replaytime EXE\n533|2; afterRestoreBranch holder/tuple/material/remote/offer/bound 1\n534|each (all EXR); refreshbound EXR 1; outcomekey REC 1 / LOOK 0 (B22\n535|singleton); binddocid REC 1 / LOOK 1; binddocshape REC 1; docpersist\n536|EXR 1; Table B verify 9 new-entry sides shared 1, server EXA 1 (its\n537|other sides are first-leaf symmetry).\n538|\n539|Ratio: 208 measured of 4448 (50+10+148 M across Tables A/B/D;\n540|Table C all U); 34 bound; 4206 unreachable with reasons. Every\n541|driven refusal direction is measured except the bound cells: 22\n542|driven but rowless (B22 singletons/forks, B23 normalized details,\n543|B29 poll past-deadline, B32 propagation) and 8 named undriven gaps\n544|(B24/B25/B26/B28/B31 cells, B29 dispatch side), each with its owner\n545|below.\n546|\n547|## Stated bounds\n548|\n549|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n550|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n551|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n552|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n553|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n554|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n555|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n556|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n557|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n558|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n559|  panic kill.\n560|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n561|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n562|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n563|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n564|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n565|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n566|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n567|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n568|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n569|  final leaf; this leaf documents clause coverage here and in the\n570|  conformance matrix only.\n571|- B9 Adapter split: this leaf ships the decision core and argv only. No\n572|  production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree; the\n573|  exec/probe adapters that report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence verdicts\n574|  and spawn through the built argv, and the server socket's crash\n575|  evidence, are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz. The\n576|  no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through Dependencies.Spawn;\n577|  a fallback through a direct os/exec call is excluded today only by\n578|  the import census (no os/exec import in the package).\n579|  Dependencies.Spawn is inert on the background path: a nil spawner\n580|  with a live broker still contacts (the broker path never calls it),\n581|  so the field is dead weight there — which is what makes the\n582|  shared-Dependencies fallback shape realistic, and why the spy\n583|  census arms the foreground probe alongside the spawner.\n584|- B10 Crash convergence assumes a umask that preserves owner rwx\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
