{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ffcf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c765-6a15-7930-81af-9d81d9b3108a"},"sequence":7746,"recorded_at":1780531400015487,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eb24712a-98eb-41ba-85bf-fe73b2577481"},"call_id":"call_01a0c7b35317706ba5f34a3683baba1b","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/wrapper.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"time\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axpane\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminstance\"\n12|)\n13|\n14|// This file orders the §4.2 after-restore sequence at the wrapper\n15|// composition entry: read the latest locally known lease, attempt the\n16|// mesh lease refresh under the measured bound, then decide through\n17|// the landed wrapper owner and route to the decided effects. The\n18|// backend restore entry stays the narrow §4.C row — recreate the\n19|// wrapper under restore authorization and return the parked wire\n20|// result — while this entry owns the order: the refresh runs before\n21|// the decision, so a lapsed local grant under a refreshed remote\n22|// winner offers remote attach instead of refusing at backend\n23|// authorization that the offer path never reaches. Backend restore\n24|// authorization is never weakened to make that path pass: the offer\n25|// and park branches run no backend operation at all.\n26|\n27|// WrapperRestoreRequest is one after-restore composition: the wrapper\n28|// decision input the caller built (mode restore), the local fencing\n29|// facts the ordered observation carries, and the backend restore\n30|// request the resume branches execute.\n31|type WrapperRestoreRequest struct {\n32|\t// Decide is the complete wrapper decision input. Mode must be\n33|\t// restore; Observation is ordered here (the caller-supplied one\n34|\t// is replaced by the refreshed/local observation), every other\n35|\t// member passes through to the landed owner.\n36|\tDecide axpane.Input\n37|\t// Grant is the process-local fencing authorization with its\n38|\t// policy, observed over the ordered winner. Presence is\n39|\t// required; expiry is the landed direction-first arm's verdict,\n40|\t// so a lapsed grant under a remote winner still parks remote\n41|\t// instead of refusing.\n42|\tGrant    sessrepo.FencingGrant\n43|\tHasGrant bool\n44|\tPolicy   sessrepo.FencingPolicy\n45|\t// Restore is the backend restore request the launch and reattach\n46|\t// branches execute. Operation must be restore; the entry\n47|\t// executes nothing else.\n48|\tRestore OpRequest\n49|}\n50|\n51|// WrapperRestoreOutcome is one composed after-restore result: the\n52|// ordered decision, the refresh audit, the winner the decision ran\n53|// over, and the backend restore outcome on the resume branches only.\n54|type WrapperRestoreOutcome struct {\n55|\t// Decision is the landed wrapper verdict: launch, reattach,\n56|\t// attach_remote, takeover_offer, parked, or refused.\n57|\tDecision axpane.Decision\n58|\t// RefreshAttempted reports that the mesh refresh ran; RefreshSucceeded\n59|\t// reports that it answered (a missing adapter, a failed attempt, and\n60|\t// a timed-out attempt all fall back to local knowledge unverified).\n61|\tRefreshAttempted bool\n62|\tRefreshSucceeded bool\n63|\t// RefreshBoundMs is the measured bound one attempt ran under.\n64|\tRefreshBoundMs uint64\n65|\t// WinnerLeaseID and WinnerHostID name the winning lease the\n66|\t// decision ran over: the refreshed winner, or the locally known\n67|\t// lease when the refresh did not answer.\n68|\tWinnerLeaseID string\n69|\tWinnerHostID  string\n70|\t// Restore is the backend restore outcome on launch and reattach,\n71|\t// nil on every other branch (those branches run no backend\n72|\t// operation and launch no provider).\n73|\tRestore *OpOutcome\n74|}\n75|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
